# Fixed defect 2373, 2026-11-09, lane b26-misc, the issue's own reproducer: in
# the package `core`'s own file, `use text/strs` and a local `strs` taking
# its name.
#
# SYMPTOM: `unused_binding` said `use <core>/text/strs` is never used, and
# `shadowed_binding`'s note said to write `use <core>/text/strs as <other>`:
# the compilation's name for the module, a line the file never wrote, and
# written there it is refused `unknown_entry`, a package's own modules being
# written bare in its files.
#
# FIX: both quote the line as the file writes it, `use text/strs`.
use <core>/strings

function main()
    print(strings.hello())
